1
00:00:19,333 --> 00:00:20,625
The teacher's coming!

2
00:00:57,416 --> 00:00:58,625
You're finally awake.

3
00:00:59,791 --> 00:01:01,375
How are you feeling?

4
00:01:02,333 --> 00:01:04,125
Does your head still hurt?

5
00:01:04,125 --> 00:01:05,000
I'm fine.

6
00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:10,250
Did the teacher come by?

7
00:01:10,791 --> 00:01:12,625
If you're that scared,

8
00:01:12,625 --> 00:01:14,375
then quit smoking.

9
00:01:14,750 --> 00:01:16,250
Are you trying
to kill yourself?

10
00:01:17,916 --> 00:01:19,291
I told him

11
00:01:19,666 --> 00:01:21,000
you didn't smoke.

12
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:25,666
Thanks.

13
00:01:25,666 --> 00:01:27,666
Don't do it again, okay?

14
00:01:27,666 --> 00:01:31,250
You'll cover for me again
next time, won't you?

15
00:01:31,250 --> 00:01:32,166
Teacher's pet.

16
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,791
You had me worried.

17
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:43,375
Thanks for worrying
about me.

18
00:01:45,666 --> 00:01:48,208
I hope it's not a bad concussion.

19
00:01:48,208 --> 00:01:50,166
Let's ask the nurse later.

20
00:01:50,875 --> 00:01:52,875
Or maybe go back
to the hospital.

21
00:01:53,708 --> 00:01:55,250
I'll stay with you.

22
00:01:56,458 --> 00:01:58,083
I've gotta get to class.

23
00:02:28,041 --> 00:02:29,041
Come on.

24
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:32,333
I've told you already.

25
00:02:32,333 --> 00:02:34,000
I don't want
cheesy clichés.

26
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,750
And you threw in
a love triangle.

27
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:37,750
Oh, please.

28
00:02:37,750 --> 00:02:40,041
Put a bunch of guys
and girls together,

29
00:02:40,041 --> 00:02:42,250
and love triangles
just happen.

30
00:02:42,250 --> 00:02:43,000
My dating show

31
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,625
is all about
what makes people shine.

32
00:02:47,166 --> 00:02:48,750
So what's your thing?

33
00:02:50,625 --> 00:02:51,875
I play piano.

34
00:02:53,291 --> 00:02:55,416
Everyone already
knows that.

35
00:02:55,416 --> 00:02:57,833
Show us
something different.

36
00:02:57,833 --> 00:02:59,833
That's what
people remember.

37
00:03:00,416 --> 00:03:01,750
I cook.

38
00:03:02,958 --> 00:03:06,041
Every guy says
he can cook.

39
00:03:06,041 --> 00:03:07,625
Not exactly unique.

40
00:03:07,916 --> 00:03:09,458
Like what?

41
00:03:11,625 --> 00:03:13,041
Buddha's Temptation,

42
00:03:13,041 --> 00:03:13,958
golden yam ring,

43
00:03:13,958 --> 00:03:17,458
braised pork belly, triple delight
sesame shrimp, salad spring rolls

44
00:03:17,458 --> 00:03:19,625
pumpkin buttermilk shrimp,
scallops with broccoli

45
00:03:19,625 --> 00:03:22,208
and shark fin soup.

46
00:03:22,208 --> 00:03:24,875
Impressive!
Where'd you learn all that?

47
00:03:25,291 --> 00:03:26,750
My dad owns a restaurant.

48
00:03:27,458 --> 00:03:30,958
I've never met a guy
who can cook like that.

49
00:03:31,583 --> 00:03:33,625
Then lunch is on you.

50
00:03:33,625 --> 00:03:35,208
We've got a staff kitchen.

51
00:03:35,208 --> 00:03:36,500
Help yourself.

52
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:37,291
Please...

53
00:03:52,375 --> 00:03:53,833
Oh, he can actually chop.

54
00:03:54,541 --> 00:03:55,333
Yeah.

55
00:03:56,458 --> 00:03:58,291
He's so hot!

56
00:03:58,291 --> 00:04:00,750
Can I be on the show?

57
00:04:02,625 --> 00:04:04,500
Cole, give me a hand.

58
00:04:12,958 --> 00:04:13,791
Huh?

59
00:04:14,583 --> 00:04:15,583
Sure.

60
00:04:17,375 --> 00:04:18,916
Grab the celery.

61
00:04:19,666 --> 00:04:21,666
Which one's the celery?

62
00:04:21,666 --> 00:04:22,875
This one.

63
00:04:33,916 --> 00:04:35,291
What are you doing?

64
00:04:36,583 --> 00:04:37,833
It's a dating show.

65
00:04:38,833 --> 00:04:40,625
It's not
just about cooking.

66
00:04:40,625 --> 00:04:43,666
I need to work
on my chemistry, too.

67
00:04:43,958 --> 00:04:45,500
Good point.

68
00:04:45,916 --> 00:04:48,416
Maybe we'll get
some good footage!

69
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:54,291
Hold it by the stem.

70
00:04:56,250 --> 00:04:57,750
Start at an angle.

71
00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:02,083
Then keep slicing.

72
00:05:02,083 --> 00:05:05,083
Look! Cole's blushing.

73
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:17,166
Thinner.

74
00:05:17,791 --> 00:05:18,791
Got it?

75
00:05:29,041 --> 00:05:29,833
Ouch!

76
00:05:32,166 --> 00:05:35,541
You can't even chop.
How are we shooting this?

77
00:05:35,541 --> 00:05:38,291
Hey, are you always this tough
on the girls?

78
00:05:40,875 --> 00:05:42,416
Are you okay?

79
00:05:42,416 --> 00:05:43,541
Let me help you.

80
00:05:52,250 --> 00:05:53,250
Are you okay?

81
00:06:11,291 --> 00:06:12,125
Prawns.

82
00:06:12,666 --> 00:06:13,625
Got it.

83
00:06:14,208 --> 00:06:15,500
Sesame.

84
00:06:16,416 --> 00:06:17,208
Alright.

85
00:06:18,125 --> 00:06:19,541
Cooking wine.

86
00:06:19,541 --> 00:06:20,333
Okay.

87
00:06:21,166 --> 00:06:21,958
Salt...

88
00:06:22,791 --> 00:06:23,916
What are you doing?

89
00:06:24,041 --> 00:06:25,916
Oh.

90
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,541
I looked up
Phil's recipes.

91
00:06:28,916 --> 00:06:32,416
This should be everything.

92
00:06:33,291 --> 00:06:35,166
Just making sure
I didn't miss anything.

93
00:06:35,791 --> 00:06:37,458
I couldn't find
the goji berries.

94
00:06:38,250 --> 00:06:39,958
Sorry. I'll go get them.

95
00:06:39,958 --> 00:06:41,250
It's okay.

96
00:06:41,583 --> 00:06:43,000
We've got enough.

97
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,125
I'll be right back.

98
00:06:44,125 --> 00:06:45,750
You don't need all this.

99
00:06:46,208 --> 00:06:47,500
We can't eat that much.

100
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:49,416
But it won't taste right.

101
00:06:50,416 --> 00:06:51,958
It's just a practice run.

102
00:06:51,958 --> 00:06:53,291
You don't have to
try so hard.

103
00:06:57,875 --> 00:06:58,500
Okay.

104
00:07:33,458 --> 00:07:35,291
Hi, I'm Jan.

105
00:07:35,291 --> 00:07:36,625
I know.

106
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:41,000
I'm a content creator.

107
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,375
I was pretty big
seven years ago.

108
00:07:44,333 --> 00:07:45,666
Now...

109
00:07:45,666 --> 00:07:47,625
I'm yesterday's news.

110
00:07:47,625 --> 00:07:48,791
I know.

111
00:07:51,041 --> 00:07:53,666
I'm one of the contestants.

112
00:07:54,791 --> 00:07:56,541
Can we talk?

113
00:07:57,583 --> 00:07:59,041
About what?

114
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,541
Don't people
on these shows

115
00:08:02,541 --> 00:08:04,833
usually have a match?

116
00:08:04,833 --> 00:08:06,458
Why don't we team up?

117
00:08:06,958 --> 00:08:08,958
Older women
are in right now.

118
00:08:09,750 --> 00:08:11,833
We'd make a great pair.

119
00:08:13,291 --> 00:08:15,583
You're just chasing clout.

120
00:08:15,583 --> 00:08:18,375
You're right.
I want the exposure.

121
00:08:20,791 --> 00:08:22,833
That's why
I'm offering a deal.

122
00:08:22,833 --> 00:08:25,333
I've got something
to offer, too.

123
00:08:26,250 --> 00:08:27,500
Don't I?

124
00:08:32,750 --> 00:08:35,291
I know you hate the hype.

125
00:08:36,291 --> 00:08:38,708
Everyone who comes to you

126
00:08:38,708 --> 00:08:40,583
just wants your clout.

127
00:08:40,583 --> 00:08:42,041
I'm different.

128
00:08:42,041 --> 00:08:44,541
I know the right people.

129
00:08:45,416 --> 00:08:47,041
I can introduce you

130
00:08:47,041 --> 00:08:49,500
to real music producers.

131
00:08:51,791 --> 00:08:52,416
Interested?

132
00:08:58,083 --> 00:09:00,583
I can't promise
they'll sign you.

133
00:09:00,875 --> 00:09:03,375
I can only introduce you.

134
00:09:04,250 --> 00:09:07,083
What happens after that

135
00:09:07,916 --> 00:09:09,958
is up to your talent.

136
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,625
So what's the deal?

137
00:09:21,541 --> 00:09:22,333
Wow.

138
00:09:22,750 --> 00:09:26,000
I had this
whole pitch ready.

139
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,458
Didn't think
it'd be that easy.

140
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:32,583
Smoke?

141
00:09:32,875 --> 00:09:33,416
I don't.

142
00:09:33,416 --> 00:09:35,291
Sorry. No smoking.
